      "lineNbr": 126,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002135
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-24T08:04:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No — this change is only for a target with its own address on a BMC-attached I2C/I3C bus. `AssignEndpointStatic` fails if the same physical address already has a different EID assigned, which is exactly the shape a bridge and the devices behind it take, so it can\u0027t express those. Endpoints reached through a bridge are a separate case, now handled by [94538] via `MCTPRoutedEndpoint` + `Network1.LearnEndpoint`. I\u0027ve reworded the commit message to make that split explicit.\n\n[94538]: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/dbus-sensors/+/94538",
      "parentUuid": "ba5080a0_a70b0a3f",
      "revId": "4535998590234969adb4ad58c1fb89d1ffaaf006",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
    },
