      "writtenOn": "2026-09-24T08:04:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Added to the commit message: unit tests now cover absent/numeric/decimal/hexadecimal/malformed/reserved/out-of-range `StaticEndpointID` values. On real Yosemite 4 hardware (I3C), mctpreactor assigned all eight direct Sentinel Dome endpoints their configured EIDs (10 through 80) and created the expected `configured_by` associations; EID 10 was recreated correctly after `Endpoint1.Remove`. I haven\u0027t had an I2C target with `StaticEndpointID` to test against — happy to if you know of one in-tree. Bridged endpoints are out of scope for this change; they\u0027re covered (and tested) separately in [94538].\n\n[94538]: https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/dbus-sensors/+/94538",
      "parentUuid": "e9ca0d57_69597a63",
      "revId": "4535998590234969adb4ad58c1fb89d1ffaaf006",
      "serverId": "adbd0a64-1f21-4d83-b585-671fe73cb6e4"
